-bb0a-4c7d-a2c2-27b4dac52a18, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Gorsuch\'s Law Gap Argument, quote: So, if somebody showed up here in 1868 and established domicile, that was perfectly fine without respect to anything,\n  - id: bbfeda90-b497-4c26-b8d6-470ba61d87e3, idea_id: 25-365, title: Wang Embraces Elk While Gray Confuses Ark, quote: I embrace that part of Elk versus Wilkins\' holding.\n  - id: a1342a18-0fa7-4746-93df-57b205f4196d, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Alito\'s Iranian Boy Test, quote: A boy is born here to an Iranian father who has entered the country illegally.\n  - id: a8b53133-1e6b-4f31-9a9c-6a320a449d9b, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Jackson Demands Citizenship Precision, quote: "independently of a residence with intention to continue such residence independently of any domiciliation"?\n  - id: 96513721-ce7b-425a-a3d2-7d1ac1632b67, idea_id: 25-365, title: Barrett\'s End-Run Jurisdiction Test, quote: order to change the meaning of the Fourteenth Amendment as to unauthorized immigrants\' children, Congress can say we are not going to exercise jurisdiction.\n  - id: c43bfff2-fd76-406c-b598-d704732a9c0c, idea_id: 25-365, title: Gorsuch\'s Evolving Presence Test, quote: Congress could continually restrict who may lawfully be present more and more, and you would say that would be incorporated into it even though\n  - id: e6cd81a4-1df5-4200-90a0-4069d1eccc2d, idea_id: 25-365, title: Gorsuch Questions Sauer on Birthright Citizenship, quote: Are tribal members born today birthright citizens?\n  - id: c738cc92-90ba-4e82-a31c-684a6cf26bd1, idea_id: 25-365, title: , quote: \n  - id: af55bc36-b133-4f50-906d-c6ee28dedb7a, idea_id: 25-365, title: Sotomayor Tests Loyalty Exceptions, quote: Other than people covered by that closed set of exceptions.\n  - id: dff50ad8-5569-4253-9201-a00db6188df5, idea_id: 25-365, title: Sotomayor Challenges Domicile Assumption, quote: So you\'re asking us to overrule that case?\n  - id: 78c8c4a6-9681-4f9d-8b78-e02e56c7af92, idea_id