2026-09-02 23:28:03 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\n        You are a workflow assistant. Extract parameters for the intent "select_asset_def_by_reference".\n\n        User message:\n        selec this asset def: Justice Gorsuch\'s Law Gap Argument\n\n        Parameter schema for this intent:\n        - "reference": type=string, required=True\n\n        Extraction instructions for this intent:\n        - The "reference" parameter must always be set to the asset\'s "title" field.\n- Never return the idea_id or quote.\n- Use the relevant context block (which lists ideas with idea_id, title, quote)\n  to determine which asset the user is referring to.\n\n\n\nRelevant context:\nasset_definitions:\n  - id: 67e23648-37fa-456a-9161-481895e5608a, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Gorsuch\'s Marital Status Carousel, quote: What if they\'re unmarried? Who -- whose domicile?\n  - id: ce82cb1e-197e-4aa4-bc78-eed424d33741, idea_id: 25-365, title: Mississippi Slave Domicile Paradox, quote: nope, you still live here. Right? And so it would be astonishing,\n  - id: fa53d988-c4f5-40ea-b166-6deeb7c07d80, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Harlan\'s Gout Springs Hypothetical, quote: Suppose an English father and mother went down to the hot springs to get rid of the gout, and while there, they have a\n  - id: 8b9d3b12-facf-4fdb-b7b5-c66cf99bdab3, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Barrett\'s Foundling Parentage Test, quote: What if you don\'t know who the parents are?\n  - id: f08ad9a2-627c-4a17-8d21-e77ac9cc3478, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Barrett\'s Norway Intent Puzzle, quote: How would you adjudicate these cases? You\'re not going to know at the time of birth for some people whether they have the intent\n  - id: 4dfefad9-9bb6-4c9d-9577-083fb9ed827b, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Barrett\'s Citizenship Reclassification Test, quote: relationship with tribal Indians has changed so much that we would say, no, Indians really are fully subject to the jurisdiction of the United\n  - id: c3e98cb0-bb0a-4c7d-a2c2-27b4dac52a18, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Gorsuch\'s Law Gap Argument, quote: So, if somebody showed up here in 1868 and established domicile, that was perfectly fine without respect to anything,\n  - id: bbfeda90-b497-4c26-b8d6-470ba61d87e3, idea_id: 25-365, title: Wang Embraces Elk While Gray Confuses Ark, quote: I embrace that part of Elk versus Wilkins\' holding.\n  - id: a1342a18-0fa7-4746-93df-57b205f4196d, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Alito\'s Iranian Boy Test, quote: A boy is born here to an Iranian father who has entered the country illegally.\n  - id: a8b53133-1e6b-4f31-9a9c-6a320a449d9b, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Jackson Demands Citizenship Precision, quote: "independently of a residence with intention to continue such residence independently of any domiciliation"?\n  - id: 96513721-ce7b-425a-a3d2-7d1ac1632b67, idea_id: 25-365, title: Barrett\'s End-Run Jurisdiction Test, quote: order to change the meaning of the Fourteenth Amendment as to unauthorized immigrants\' children, Congress can say we are not going to exercise jurisdiction.\n  - id: c43bfff2-fd76-406c-b598-d704732a9c0c, idea_id: 25-365, title: Gorsuch\'s Evolving Presence Test, quote: Congress could continually restrict who may lawfully be present more and more, and you would say that would be incorporated into it even though\n  - id: e6cd81a4-1df5-4200-90a0-4069d1eccc2d, idea_id: 25-365, title: Gorsuch Questions Sauer on Birthright Citizenship, quote: Are tribal members born today birthright citizens?\n  - id: c738cc92-90ba-4e82-a31c-684a6cf26bd1, idea_id: 25-365, title: , quote: \n  - id: af55bc36-b133-4f50-906d-c6ee28dedb7a, idea_id: 25-365, title: Sotomayor Tests Loyalty Exceptions, quote: Other than people covered by that closed set of exceptions.\n  - id: dff50ad8-5569-4253-9201-a00db6188df5, idea_id: 25-365, title: Sotomayor Challenges Domicile Assumption, quote: So you\'re asking us to overrule that case?\n  - id: 78c8c4a6-9681-4f9d-8b78-e02e56c7af92, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Barrett\'s Off-Reservation Reality Check, quote: the Indians? What about the Indian who is off the reservation or born off of a reservation?\n  - id: b09b67a5-2f4c-483a-ab6e-f5fc6b401181, idea_id: 25-365, title: Justice Kagan Demands Century-Breaking Evidence, quote: what do you think it should take to accept that story in terms of the -- the magnitude of the evidence\n  - id: 59dca59b-7a7c-42e5-b77d-72f4e3634347, idea_id: 25-365, title: , quote: \n  - id: 57ce4884-f9b5-466b-a123-9b637e388423, idea_id: 25-365, title: Government Concedes Wong Kim Ark Victory, quote: That rule was enshrined in the Fourteenth Amendment to put it out of the reach of any government official to destroy.\n  - id: c1c1ab03-af24-441d-b678-d24fc87c023d, idea_id: 25-365, title: Two Births, Two Allegiances, quote: It demeans the priceless and profound gift of American citizenship.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
